// v2p62 New Algorithm Discovery Pass 1:
// - PF remains below 1.10 and the strongest passive Pullback promise failed its v2p61 live reactivation test.
// - Pullback returns to Sidelined/shadow-only evaluation.
// - Adds two genuinely new probation candidates under the 3-6 adjustment-pass rule:
//   MomentumContinuation targets established directional persistence with stable low-noise structure.
//   ExhaustionReset targets post-expansion loss of directional coherence / reset-reversal conditions.
//
// v2p63 Probation Pass 2 / Router Discipline:
// - MomentumContinuation is narrowed toward clean short-directional persistence after its
//   only positive v2p62 pocket appeared in ShortBiasDirectional behavior.
// - ExhaustionReset is narrowed away from Transition and toward late-directional / shock
//   exhaustion where its first pass was profitable.
// - RangeReclaim is excluded from established directional states where repeated tests
//   show persistent losses; it remains a change-of-state / reclaim specialist.
// - Dormant replacement ranking now includes a decaying reactivation cooldown/history
//   penalty so recently failed live reactivations cannot immediately recycle to the top.
// - TrendRetest is narrowed toward its repeatedly positive ShockExpansion niche.
// - Existing behavior-router, confidence, relevance, profitability-potential and readiness architecture is preserved.
//
// v2p60 Dormant Replacement Readiness:
// - Keeps the v2p59 live roster unchanged so the untested roster decision is not confounded.
// - Adds persistence-aware dormant evaluation on top of RelevanceFactor and
//   ProfitabilityPotential. A sidelined sub-EA must remain relevant often enough
//   to earn a high ReplacementReadiness score rather than winning from a brief spike.
// - Tracks the fraction of observed bars where dormant relevance is materially high.
// - ReplacementReadiness combines ProfitabilityPotential, current relevance,
//   relevance persistence and shadow-sample confidence.
// - ReadinessRank provides the preferred dormant replacement shortlist while
//   ReactivationRank and ReplacementRank remain available for diagnostic comparison.
//
// v2p59 Dormant Profitability Potential + adaptive roster cycle:
// v2p61 Controlled Reactivation Test:
// - DelayedConfirmation returns to Sidelined after its v2p60 live reactivation failed.
// - Pullback returns to Probation because it ranked #1 in dormant Replacement Readiness
//   and showed enough Profitability Promise to defer mandatory new-algorithm discovery for one pass.
// - Pullback live eligibility is deliberately stricter than the other probation algorithms:
//   at least MEDIUM router confidence, stronger descriptor fit, adequate stability, and limited noise.
// - Sidelined algorithms remain impossible to route live, but continue cheap descriptor
//   relevance tracking plus sparse fixed-horizon shadow probes.
// - ProfitabilityPotential is deliberately separate from RelevanceFactor: it combines
//   market relevance, shadow expectancy/win evidence, and sample-confidence shrinkage
//   to estimate whether a sidelined algorithm could plausibly be profitable if reactivated.
// - ReplacementRank ranks sidelined algorithms by ProfitabilityPotential, while
//   ReactivationRank remains the pure current-relevance ranking.
//
// v2p58 Sidelined Relevance Monitor:
// - Sidelined sub-EAs are absolutely excluded from live routing/trading.
// - They remain lightweight virtual candidates: descriptor fit is tracked every bar,
//   and only strong hypothetical setups open a short fixed-horizon shadow probe.
// - RelevanceFactor combines current descriptor relevance with shadow-probe effectiveness,
//   providing a ranked reactivation shortlist without trade-result feedback entering live routing.
// - This design deliberately limits overhead to one shadow probe per sidelined algorithm.
//
// v2p57 Behavior Router validation/refinement:
// - Descriptor fit now dominates routing; coarse state labels are only weak priors.
// - Confidence calibration rewards descriptor separation/coherence so genuinely
//   distinctive environments can reach HIGH without broadening low-confidence trade flow.
// - Repeated specialist evidence is expressed through descriptor shape: TrendRetest
//   favors orderly expansion/shock-like behavior; CompressionRelease favors unstable
//   compression-to-release/transition behavior; Pullback favors moderate expansion
//   with stability rather than directional-state identity.
// - DelayedConfirmation is sidelined after exhausting its probation runway without
//   a stable profitable behavior specialty. Trade management remains unchanged.
//
// v2p56 Behavior Descriptor v2:
// - Replaces state-label-first routing with continuous descriptor fit.
// - Directionality, expansion, compression, noise, persistence and stability
//   are measured from candles before a specialist becomes eligible.
// - Router confidence is classified LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH and the required
//   descriptor fit rises as confidence falls; low confidence never broadens
//   eligibility merely to force a trade.
// - State labels remain logged as summaries, but descriptor fit now drives
//   specialist eligibility and ranking.
//
// v2p55 Behavior Router v1:
// - Separates market-behavior recognition from sub-EA competition.
// - Current candle statistics still determine the behavior state/confidence;
//   recent trade PnL is NOT used to decide what the market currently is.
// - The router converts behavior + confidence into an eligible specialist set,
//   then ranks only those eligible sub-EAs instead of letting every algorithm
//   compete everywhere.
// - UNKNOWN and TRANSITION remain first-class outcomes; low-confidence states
//   receive deliberately weaker routing authority rather than forced certainty.
// - State logging now records router confidence, eligible algorithms, selected
//   algorithm, and selection margin independently for long and short decisions.
// - Trade management and sub-EA internals remain unchanged from v2p54 so this
//   run measures the behavior-router architecture rather than another tuning pass.

//
// v2p64 Algorithm Discovery + Specialist Consolidation:
// - MomentumContinuation and ExhaustionReset advance to probation pass 3 after profitable v2p63 results.
